\n\
Opponent played Ostrich-Horse this turn (it's sick), milled 3 cards including Earthbender Ascension and Swampsnare Trap apparently.\n\
\n\
My options:\n\
1. Play Island (4th land), then cast Cat-Owl? Cat-Owl costs {3}{W/U} — I have Plains, Island, Island, and would play another Island = 4 mana. Cat-Owl is {3}{W/U} which means 3 generic plus W or U. So 4 mana total. I can cast it.\n\
\n\
2. Attack with both creatures. Ostrich-Horse is 3/1 and sick, so it can't block this turn (summoning sickness affects blocking? No! Summoning sickness only prevents attacking and tapping abilities. Blocking is fine). Wait, no — summoning sickness prevents attacking and using tap abilities, but a creature CAN block while summoning sick. Actually no, that's wrong. Summoning sickness prevents attacking and activating abilities with tap/untap symbols. Blocking is allowed.\n\
\n\
So Ostrich-Horse can block. It's a 3/1. If I attack with Rallier (2/2) and Jailer (3/3), opponent can block one with Ostrich-Horse (3/1). If they block Jailer, Ostrich-Horse dies and Jailer lives (3/3 takes 3 damage... wait, 3/1 deals 3 to Jailer, Jailer is 3/3 so takes 3 damage and dies? No — 3 damage to a 3/3 kills it. Both die). If they block Rallier, Ostrich-Horse kills Rallier (3 damage to 2/2) and Rallier deals 2 to Ostrich-Horse (1 toughness) — both die.\n\
\n\
Actually, trades: Ostrich-Horse 3/1 blocks anything and dies to anything with 2+ power. So opponent can trade Ostrich-Horse for either of my creatures. \n\
\n\
Alternatively, I can use Airbending Lesson to airbend the Ostrich-Horse (return it to hand? Airbend = exile, and owner can cast it for {2} less? Let me recall airbending mechanic: \"Airbend target nonland permanent\" — exiles it, and its owner may cast it from exile for as long as it remains exiled by paying {2} less? Actually in Avatar set, airbend: \"Exile it. For as long as that card remains exiled, its owner may cast it by paying {2} rather than its mana cost.\" Something like that. The card says \"Airbend target nonland permanent. : Draw a card.\" Weird formatting but it also draws a card? Let me check: \"Airbending Lesson {2}{W}: Airbend target nonland permanent. : Draw a card.\" Hmm, the \":\" might be a rendering issue. Probably \"Draw a card.\" So it's a removal-ish bounce that lets them recast for {2}.\n\
\n\
Let me think about the best play:\n\
\n\
Option A: Play Island, cast Cat-Owl (3/3 flying). Then attack with Rallier and Jailer. Opponent blocks with Ostrich-Horse, trades with one. I get in for 2 or 3.\n\
\n\
Option B: Attack first, then play Cat-Owl postcombat.\n\
\n\
Either way, attack first vs. cast first doesn't matter much since Cat-Owl is a creature. But wait — should I use Airbending Lesson on Ostrich-Horse before combat to clear the blocker? That costs {2}{W} = 3 mana, leaving me unable to cast Cat-Owl this turn (only 4 mana total after playing Island). Hmm.\n\
\n\
If I Airbending Lesson the Ostrich-Horse: it gets exiled, opponent can recast it for {2} (its mana cost minus 2? Ostrich-Horse costs... 3/1 with mill 3 ETB, probably costs {2}{G} or {3}?). Airbend lets them recast for {2} generic instead of its cost. So they can replay it and mill again. That's not great, but it does clear the way for attacks this turn and draws me a card.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, just attack into it. If they block, they trade. Trading Ostrich-Horse for my Rallier — is that good for me? They get to mill again? No, mill is ETB only. If Ostrich-Horse dies, it's gone. Trade seems fine-ish, but I'd rather keep my creatures.\n\
\n\
Actually, the better consideration: opponent has Swampsnare Trap in graveyard (already used or milled). They have 7 cards in hand. They're on G/B with Omashu City (R/G) and Foggy Bottom Swamp (B/G).\n\
\n\
