      "reasoning": "I'm on turn 4 precombat with my 4th land already down. My board is Rallier (2/2) + Jailer (3/3) against their summoning-sick Ostrich-Horse (3/1) — note it *can* block despite being sick. All their lands are tapped, so no tricks. I'll move to combat to attack with both.",
      "thinking": "It's my turn 4 precombat main. My plan from the log: play my 4th land (Island — wait, I already have 3 Islands and 1 Plains in play; looking at the board, I have Island p6, p7, p27, Plains p8 all untapped. So the land was already played this turn? Let me check: battlefield shows 4 lands untapped. Turn 4, active player me, priority me, precombat main. It seems I already played the Island (p27) this turn. Actually from the log: \"Playing my 4th land (Island), then I'll attack with both and cast Cat-Owl postcombat.\" So land is played.\n\
\n\
