\n\
Opponent at 18. If I attack with both, they can block one with Ostrich-Horse (3/1). If they block Jailer (3/3), Ostrich-Horse dies and Jailer survives (3 damage to 3/3? No — Ostrich-Horse deals 3 to Jailer, Jailer is 3/3, so Jailer dies too; Jailer deals 3 to Ostrich-Horse 3/1, it dies). Trade 3/3 for 3/1 — bad for me? Actually trading Jailer for Ostrich-Horse... Ostrich-Horse already did its ETB. Jailer has a useful ETB but it's already on board. Trading 3/3 for 3/1 is generally unfavorable stat-wise but killing their only creature... Hmm.\n\
\n\
If they block Rallier (2/2): Ostrich-Horse 3/1 kills Rallier, Rallier deals 2 to Ostrich-Horse killing it. Trade 2/2 for 3/1 — favorable-ish.\n\
\n\
They'll choose which to block. They'd probably block Jailer to trade up? Or block Rallier to kill it and trade. Either way Ostrich-Horse likely dies if they block. They might not block at all and take 5, going to 13.\n\
