Should I attack with both? Yes. Then postcombat cast Cat-Owl (3W/U — I have W UUU, so yes 4 mana). That leaves no mana for anything else.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, cast Cat-Owl precombat? No reason; postcombat is fine, and attacking first is better.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — should I consider holding back Jailer to avoid the trade? If they block Jailer with Ostrich-Horse, both die. Is that bad for me? I have Cat-Owl coming. Trading Jailer for their only creature... my board would be Rallier + Cat-Owl vs their nothing. That's fine. But trading 3/3 for 3/1 where I could instead just... if I attack with only Rallier, they block with Ostrich-Horse, both die? Rallier 2/2 vs 3/1: both die. Then I keep Jailer. Hmm, that's also reasonable.\n\
\n\
But if I attack with both and they don't block, they take 5. If they block, I likely trade one creature for Ostrich-Horse and get 2-3 damage through. Attacking with both is the aggressive on-the-play play and I'm ahead. They milled cards and are playing a value game; I should press.\n\
\n\
Actually, let's think: is the trade of Jailer for Ostrich-Horse good? Ostrich-Horse is a 3/1 that milled them value. My Jailer is a 3/3 with an ETB already used. Board after trade: Rallier 2/2 + Cat-Owl 3/3 flyer vs their empty board. That's great for me. Attack with both.\n\
\n\
