- 6 cards in hand\n\
- Graveyard: Earthbender Ascension, Ostrich-Horse, Swampsnare Trap\n\
\n\
Interesting — opponent has a Phoenix Fleet Airship but no creatures to crew it with. They have 4 lands, all tapped from their turn 4.\n\
\n\
Turn 5 for me. Options:\n\
1. Cast Waterbending Lesson ({3}{U}): Draw 3, discard 1 unless I waterbend {2}. If I pay 4 total ({3}{U} plus waterbend {2} = 6 total... wait, waterbend {2} means paying 2 more). Actually \"discard a card unless you waterbend {2}\" — so either pay {2} extra or discard a card. I have 4 mana, so casting it for {3}{U} leaves 0, so I'd have to discard a card. That's fine — drawing 3 and discarding 1 is still +2 cards effectively.\n\
\n\
2. Cast second Cat-Owl ({3}{W/U}): I have 3 Islands + 1 Plains = {W}{U}{U}{U}, so I can pay {3}{W/U} with W from Plains and the rest. That gives me two 3/3 fliers. Strong clock.\n\
\n\
3. Attack first with Cat-Owl and Rallier, then decide postcombat.\n\
\n\
The Cat-Owl attack trigger: \"Whenever this attacks, untap target artifact or creature.\" That could untap a land? No — artifact or creature only. Could untap Rallier after attacking? Attacking taps Rallier... actually I attack with both, Cat-Owl's trigger can untap Rallier. Not super useful precombat.\n\
\n\
Opponent's board: no creatures. The Airship needs crew 1 but they have no creatures. So my attack is basically free unless they play something at instant speed. They have 6 cards in hand but all lands tapped... wait, it's my turn now, so their lands untap on their turn. Actually it says their lands are tapped — that means on their turn 4 they tapped everything (to cast Phoenix Fleet Airship presumably, which costs... probably 4-5 mana).\n\
\n\
Wait, if all their lands are tapped, then it's currently... let me re-read. It's Turn 5 PRECOMBAT_MAIN for me. Their lands show tapped — hmm, that's odd since they should untap at the start of their turn... unless the snapshot is showing their lands still tapped from their last turn? No wait — if it's my turn 5, their turn 4 just ended, and their lands would remain tapped through my turn? No! Lands untap at the beginning of each player's own turn. So on my turn 5, their lands from their turn 4... no wait, they untap on THEIR turn, so after their turn 4 ends, lands stay tapped until their turn 5 untap step. Right — during my turn, their lands are still tapped from their turn. So they have no mana available this turn. \n\
\n\
So they can't cast anything this turn (unless 0-cost). My attack is safe.\n\
\n\
Plan: Attack with Cat-Owl and Rallier for 5 in the air/ground. They have no blockers (Airship isn't a creature unless crewed, and they have no creatures to crew). So 5 damage gets through: 16 → 11.\n\
\n\
Then postcombat, cast second Cat-Owl (4 mana: Plains + 3 Islands... {3}{W/U} = 3 generic + W or U. Plains pays W, three Islands pay 3 generic. Yes). That leaves 0 mana.\n\
\n\
Alternatively, cast Waterbending Lesson to draw 3 and discard 1. But curving the second Cat-Owl gives a massive air clock: two 3/3 fliers + 2/2 ground = 8 damage per turn. Opponent at 11 after this attack, then dead in ~2 turns.\n\
\n\
Also consider: should I hold Cat-Owl and cast Waterbending Lesson to dig for lands? I have 4 lands and a 4-mana hand full of spells. If I cast Cat-Owl, I'm tapped out with Airbending Lesson + 2x Waterbending Lesson in hand. Next turn I draw — if it's a land, I can cast Waterbending Lesson with waterbend. Hmm.\n\
\n\
The opponent's deck seems to be B/G/r/g with sacrifice synergy (Phoenix Fleet Airship wants sacrifices). They have Swampsnare Trap in graveyard (enchant creature -5/-3, costs 1 less targeting flier) — that's an answer to my Cat-Owls. If they draw another one or have one in hand, they can kill a Cat-Owl. But they can't crew the Airship without creatures.\n\
\n\
Best play: attack with both, then cast second Cat-Owl. Double flier clock is the fastest path to winning. They're at 16; after attack 11; next turn attack for 8 (two Cat-Owls + Rallier) → 3; then dead.\n\
\n\
Actually wait — should I attack with Rallier too? If they have no blockers, yes, free 2 damage. The Airship can't block (not a creature). Unless they crew it — but crew requires tapping a creature, and they have none. So yes, attack with both.\n\
\n\
Also consider using Airbending Lesson on their Airship precombat? Airbend target nonland permanent — that would... airbend probably exiles and returns it or something. Let me check the oracle text. \"Airbend target nonland permanent. Draw a card.\" Airbending in ATLA set: exiles the permanent, and its owner may cast it for {2}... Actually in the Avatar set, airbend = \"Exile it. For as long as it remains exiled, its owner may cast it by paying {2} rather than its mana cost.\" Something like that. Not worth spending 3 mana on now; better to develop.\n\
\n\
Sequencing: Attack first (declare attackers), then postcombat cast Cat-Owl. Let me do that.\n\
\n\
Actually, one consideration: should I cast Cat-Owl precombat so it can attack? No — it would be summoning sick. Casting postcombat is correct.\n\
\n\
Also, should I hold back Rallier to avoid... no, no blockers,free damage.\n\
\n\
Let me attack with both.",
