\n\
Lands: 5 Islands + 1 Plains = 6 mana.\n\
\n\
Opponent has 6 lands (all tapped except... actually all tapped this turn; they'll untap on their turn). They have 4 cards in hand. The Rise of Sozin at lore 1.\n\
\n\
Plan: Play Katara now (2U). Then maybe cast Waterbending Lesson to draw 3 and discard 1 (no waterbend since no creatures... wait, waterbend 2 requires tapping creatures? Waterbend costs can be paid by tapping untapped creatures/artifacts you control, paying 1 for each? Actually waterbend {N} is an additional cost you can pay with mana or by tapping... Hmm, waterbend is a cost that can be paid with mana, and you can tap untapped creatures/artifacts to help pay (each contributes 1). Since Katara would be summoning sick, can't tap her.\n\
\n\
Actually simpler: I have 6 mana. Katara costs 3 (2U). Waterbending Lesson costs 4 (3U). I can cast both this turn: 3+4=7 > 6. So I can cast Katara + pay waterbend 2 for the Lesson? Waterbending Lesson: \"Draw three cards. Then discard a card unless you waterbend {2}.\" Waterbend {2} means as you cast it you may pay an additional {2} (which can be paid by tapping creatures/artifacts each for 1 generic). So total: Katara (3) + Lesson (4) + waterbend (2) = 9 > 6. Not possible.\n\
\n\
Options:\n\
A) Cast Katara only (3 mana), leave 3 up. Opponent at 6, empty board. Katara starts clocking. But Katara is 2/3; at end step if tapped, gets +1/+1 counter. I could attack next turn.\n\
\n\
B) Cast Waterbending Lesson (4 mana), draw 3, discard 1. Leaves 2 mana. Digs for more threats/answers.\n\
\n\
C) Cast Katara, then attack... Katara is summoning sick, can't attack this turn.\n\
\n\
Opponent is at 6 with an empty board and a Saga ticking. Chapter II will exile cards from my hand/graveyard/library with a chosen name — annoying but not devastating. Chapter III transforms into Fire Lord Sozin, a creature.\n\
\n\
I think developing Katara is the priority — I need a clock since they wiped the board. Then next turn I can cast Waterbending Lesson with waterbend paid by tapping Katara (if she survives... she'll attack and tap).\n\
\n\
Actually, wait — should I also consider casting Waterbending Lesson now and discarding? I have 6 mana; Lesson costs 4, leaving 2. Can't cast Katara after. Draw 3 discard 1 nets +2 cards. Katara in hand already; digging could find better threats. But Katara is a fine threat and puts pressure. With opponent at 6, pressure matters most. Also Katara's waterbend {6}: draw a card — late game value.\n\
\n\
Sequencing: play Katara now. Then hold the Lessons. Next turn (turn 8), I'll have 7 mana: attack with Katara (taps, gets counter at end step), then cast Waterbending Lesson paying waterbend 2 by tapping... wait, can I tap Katara for waterbend while she's attacking/tapped? Waterbend requires untapped creatures. If she attacks, she's tapped. Hmm, but I could tap another creature... I only have Katara. So waterbend 2 = pay 2 mana, or tap Katara + pay 1. If Katara attacks she's tapped, so I'd pay 2 mana normally. 7 mana: Lesson 4 + waterbend 2 = 6, leaving 1. That works.\n\
\n\
Also, note Katara's ability: \"At the beginning of your end step, if Katara is tapped, put a +1/+1 counter on her.\" So attacking grows her.\n\
\n\
One concern: opponent might have removal for Katara (Swampsnare Trap is in graveyard; they could have more). They're at 6, so they need to answer pressure. Fire Lord Sozin will be a creature after chapter III.\n\
\n\
Also should I consider holding Katara and casting Lesson first to dig? If I cast Lesson now: draw 3, discard 1 (unless I pay 2 extra — I can't afford both Lesson+waterbend+Katara). Discard probably a second Lesson or a land... I have no extra lands in hand. I'd discard a Lesson probably. Then I've spent 4 mana, 2 left, can't cast Katara. That leaves my board empty for another turn and lets them develop. Not great. Katara now is better: board presence, clock.\n\
\n\
Decision: Cast Katara, Bending Prodigy now. Mana: tap 2 Islands + ... cost {2}{U}: tap Plains? No, need U. Tap 2 Islands for {2}{U}? {2}{U} = one blue + two generic. Tap 3 lands: Island (U) + Island + Island (or Plains). Fine, auto-tap.\n\
\n\
Then pass. Actually, wait — should I also cast Waterbending Lesson after Katara? 6-3=3 mana left, Lesson costs 4. No.\n\
\n\
So: cast Katara, then pass turn.\n\
\n\
Let me also think about the chapter II: opponent will name a card to exile from my hand/gy/library. Likely names Cat-Owl (2 in my graveyard, more in library?) or whatever. Not much I can do about it.\n\
