\n\
They're at 6. My clock: Katara 2/3 — they have Bumi 5/4 and Mountain 4/4 as potential blockers. Katara doesn't have evasion. I need to find something in the draw-3 to close the game: maybe another flier (Cat-Owl), or removal, or something.\n\
\n\
Decision: Cast Waterbending Lesson now, precombat, to dig. With 7 lands, tap 4, keep 3 up. Then decide based on draws.\n\
\n\
Also consider: should I attack with Katara first? If I attack into Bumi/Mountain, they just block and kill Katara (Bumi 5/4 kills 2/3, Bumi survives with 4 toughness vs 2 power). Bad. So no attack; Katara stays back as a blocker.\n\
\n\
Cast Waterbending Lesson: I'll pay {3}{U} with lands. Auto-tap is fine — it'll tap 4 lands leaving 3. But which lands matter: Agna Qel'a has an activated ability {2}{U},{T}: draw a card, discard a card. If I leave Agna + 2 Islands untapped, I could activate it later. Let me specify mana plan: tap Plains p8, Island p6, p7, p27 for the Lesson (that's {3}{U}: three generic + one blue). Leave Islands p45, p56 and Agna Qel'a p62 untapped. Then if needed, Agna Qel'a can loot.\n\
\n\
Actually, let me auto-tap but ensure it leaves what I want. Auto-tap might tap Agna Qel'a. Better to give explicit mana_plan: \"p8,p6,p7,p27\" — Plains + 3 Islands = WUUU, cost {3}{U} = 3 generic + U. Fine.\n\
\n\
Then after drawing 3, the waterbend {2} choice: I can tap Katara for {1}... hmm, does waterbend tap one permanent per {1}? Let me get the reminder text. Katara's \"Waterbend {6}: Draw a card\" — to activate, pay {6} or tap creatures/artifacts totaling... If each tap pays {1}, then waterbend {6} needs 6 taps or mix of mana+taps. That seems like a lot. Alternatively waterbend might be: \"tap an untapped creature or artifact you control rather than pay this cost\" entirely — one tap pays all generic? That seems too strong for {6}.\n\
\n\
Let me look up the mechanic reminder text via oracle on a card that has full reminder. The game state strips reminder text. I recall from the Avatar: The Last Airbender set spoilers: Waterbend is \"You may tap an untapped artifact or creature you control rather than pay this spell's/ability's generic mana cost\" — I think each waterbend N is a cost where you can tap any number, each contributing {1}. Like \"convoke\" but for generic only and includes artifacts.\n\
\n\
Hmm, actually I recall the Aang set mechanics: Airbend (exile, return by paying {2}), Waterbend (tap artifacts/creatures to help pay costs — each taps for {1}), Earthbend (land becomes creature with counters), Firebending (add mana when attacking). Yes, waterbend = convoke variant: \"For each generic mana in this cost, you may tap an untapped artifact or creature you control rather than pay that mana.\" Something like that.\n\
\n\
So for Waterbending Lesson's \"discard unless you waterbend {2}\": I can tap Katara ({1}) + pay {1} mana, or tap Katara + another artifact/creature (I have none other), or just pay {2} with lands, or discard a card.\n\
\n\
With 3 lands left after casting, paying {2} leaves 1 land. Or tap Katara + 1 land. Tapping Katara gives her a counter at end step — nice, she becomes 3/4, better blocker against Bumi trample (still 2 trample through... 5 power vs 4 toughness → 1 trample). Hmm.\n\
\n\
But wait — if I tap Katara for waterbend, she's tapped and can't block this turn... but it's my turn; blocking matters on opponent's turn. She'll untap on my next upkeep. Opponent attacks on their turn 9 — Katara would still be tapped from waterbending on my turn 8! No wait — untap step: I untap at the start of my turn 9? No! My turn 8 end step → opponent's turn 9 → Katara remains tapped through opponent's turn 9. She can't block on their turn 9. That's bad if I need blockers.\n\
\n\
Hold on: tapping Katara on my turn means she stays tapped until my next untap step (start of my turn 9, after opponent's turn). So she can't block Bumi on their turn. But she gets a +1/+1 counter at my end step (consolation). Blocking value: 2/3 chump on Bumi (trample 2 through) or block Mountain 4/4 (Katara dies, no trample, prevent 4). That's significant.\n\
\n\
Alternative: pay {2} with lands for the waterbend, keep Katara untapped as blocker. I have 7 lands; cast Lesson (4), pay waterbend {2} (2 more) = 6, leaving 1 land untapped. Fine — I wasn't going to use more mana anyway unless I draw something castable with 1 mana. Drawing 3 first, then deciding: if I draw a 1-2 mana play, having lands up matters. The discard-vs-waterbend choice happens after drawing, so I can decide then.\n\
\n\
Actually sequencing: cast Lesson → draw 3 → choose waterbend {2} or discard. If I draw good cheap cards, maybe discard instead and keep mana. If I draw nothing useful, pay {2} (lands) to keep cards, keep Katara untapped.\n\
\n\
Also consider Agna Qel'a looting: {2}{U},{T} draw then discard. With 3 lands untapped after Lesson, I could loot once. Might be better than waterbending {2}: loot to dig deeper? Waterbend {2} uses 2 mana, loot uses 3 mana ({2}{U}). Can't do both with 3 untapped. Depends on draws.\n\
\n\
Let me just cast the Lesson now and see. The pending action: I have priority in precombat main. Playable: two Waterbending Lessons. Choose p24 with mana plan leaving Agna + 2 Islands? Which lands to leave: I want Agna Qel'a (loot) + Islands for blue. Keep p62 (Agna), p45, p56 untapped; tap p8 (Plains), p6, p7, p27.\n\
\n\
mana_plan format: \"p8,p6,p7,p27\". The cost {3}{U}: system will allocate. Good.\n\
\n\
