Rule: A creature with summoning sickness can't attack, and its activated abilities with {T} can't be activated. But convoke tapping: \"302.6. A creature's activated ability with the tap symbol in its activation cost can't be activated unless the creature has been under its controller's control continuously since their most recent turn began.\" Convoke taps creatures NOT via their own abilities — convoke CAN tap summoning sick creatures? No! Convoke cannot tap summoning-sick creatures... Hmm, actually YES it can? Let me think. Convoke: \"For each colored mana in this spell's total cost, you may tap an untapped creature of that color you control rather than pay that mana.\" Can you tap a summoning-sick creature for convoke? YES, you can! Summoning sickness only prevents attacking and activating {T} abilities. Convoke is not the creature's ability — it's the spell's ability. So you CAN tap summoning-sick creatures for convoke. Similarly waterbend (which works like convoke: \"you may tap an untapped creature rather than pay {1}\") can tap summoning-sick creatures.\n\
