With Katara (7 life): Turn 9 — 7 lands untap + Katara. Draw a card. Plays: Lesson {3}{U} tapping Katara for waterbend {2} → draw 3, no discard. Then 3 mana left: Aang {3}{W}. Board: Katara 2/3 (tapped → 3/4 at end step), Aang 3/2. Attack with Aang? They have Wasp 2/2 flying blocker + others. Aang ETB airbend: target Bumi (most dangerous, costs {2} to recast) or Sozin ({2} to recast — wait, Sozin is the transformed Saga; airbending it exiles it, they recast for {2} as Fire Lord Sozin? Hmm, the back face casting — when exiled, can they cast the back face for {2}? The airbend permission lets them cast \"that card\" — front face is The Rise of Sozin {4}{B}{B}... transformed permanent exiled: it becomes the front face in exile? A double-faced card in exile is its front face characteristics... but the card can't be cast as back face. Airbend says cast for {2} rather than its mana cost — front face Rise of Sozin has mana cost {4}{B}{B}, so they could recast the SAGA for {2}?! That would wipe the board again (chapter I)! Oh no — airbending Sozin gives them a re-castable Rise of Sozin for {2} which destroys all creatures again. TERRIBLE. Never airbend Sozin.\n\
\n\
So Aang ETB targets Bumi (recast {2}, ETB earthbend 4 again — another 4/4 land! also bad-ish, but at least no board wipe) or Wasp (recast {2}, ETB sacrifice-draw maybe) or Airship if recast. Hmm, all their creatures have ETB value. Airbending Bumi: they recast for {2}, earthbend 4 again → new 4/4 land. Ugh.\n\
\n\
OK the game looks really hard. But let's just maximize: keep Katara, take the damage, dig hard. Actually, hmm, wait — one more idea for turn 9: Agna Qel'a looting {2}{U}: draw/discard. With 7 lands: Lesson (4) + loot (3) = 7 mana, Katara taps for waterbend. Draw 3 + loot + draw step = 5 new cards seen turn 9. Good digging.\n\
\n\
Also: Katara's own waterbend {6}: draw a card. Turn 9: {6} via Katara tap (2) + 4 mana. So: Lesson (4 mana + Katara tap) leaves 3 mana — not 4. Alternatively skip Lesson: Katara waterbend {6} (tap Katara + 4 mana) draw 1, leaves 3 mana for Aang. Meh, Lesson is better (draw 3).\n\
\n\
Fine. Decision now: don't block. Take 9 → 11. Then in extra combat, decide whether Katara blocks Mountain.\n\
\n\
Let me now decide the extra-combat decision in advance: 7 life + Katara vs 11 life. Given their turn-10 alpha is ~16-20 damage, 11 vs 7 barely matters (both dead without drawn help); Katara is a real blocker + engine. I'll keep Katara: take 4 in extra combat, stay at 7.\n\
\n\
Hmm wait, actually, let me reconsider whether they even get the extra combat: Bumi must deal combat damage to a player. If I don't block Bumi, yes 5 damage → trigger. Unavoidable (blocking Katara under Bumi still tramples 3 through → still trigger). So extra combat happens regardless.\n\
\n\
One more crazy idea: block Bumi with Katara AND activate... no, no mana. OK.\n\
\n\
Also, should I consider that at 7 life, they might just burn me out? They have Firebending mana etc. Unknown hand. Risk accepted.\n\
\n\
Also chat: opponent is chatty. I should reply — it's been a while. Send a good-natured message acknowledging the comeback.\n\
\n\
Let me act: no blocks (choice=\"no\"), with summary + rationale. Then handle the extra combat decision when it comes.\n\
\n\
Actually — wait. Let me double-check the no-block line once more. First combat: Mountain 4 + Bumi 5 = 9 → 20-9 = 11. Bumi trigger: untap all their lands, extra combat (land creatures only). Extra combat: Mountain attacks (4/4). If no block: 11-4 = 7. Then their postcombat main: 6 mana available, 4 cards in hand — they may deploy more threats. Then my turn 9 at 7 life.\n\
\n\
vs blocking Mountain with Katara in extra combat: stay 11, Katara dead.\n\
\n\
I'll go with no blocks all the way, keeping Katara at 7 life. Katara then grows: wait — if Katara is untapped at my end step, no counter. My end step is past anyway; it's their turn. Katara stays 2/3 until my turn 9 end step (she'll be tapped from waterbend payment → becomes 3/4).\n\
\n\
