What about Crashing Wave X=3 (skip Momo)? Then turn 9: all 4 lands + Katara for Wave X=3. Tap Sozin + Wasp + Zookeeper (or any 3), stun Bumi, Mountain, Sozin. Attackers turn 9: Wasp + Zookeeper. Katara untapped (if I tap lands for waterbend instead of Katara)! Crashing Wave X=3: UU (Agna + Island) + waterbend {3} = Plains + Plains + Katara? That's 3. OR 3 lands... I only have 2 Plains left after UU. So waterbend {3} = Plains + Plains + Katara tap. Katara tapped → can't block. Same as before but no Momo. Blockers: none! Take 8 → dead. ✗✗. So X=3 without Momo = death. X=2 + Momo is THE line. (X=2 leaves 1 Plains for Momo.)\n\
\n\
Wait, actually, could I do X=2 with waterbend paid by Katara + Plains, last Plains for Momo — yes that's Line B. ✓. Or X=2 paid by 2 Plains, Katara untapped → no Momo, Katara blocks: block Zookeeper (Katara 2/3 dies), take 4 from Wasp → 3. Turn 10: no Momo → Aang costs {3}{W} (no discount): Aang {3}{W} + Flyer {1}{U} + Deserters {1}{W} = 8 mana (3W 1U + 4 gen) — 3W needed, have 2W ✗. Aang {3}{W} + Flyer = 6 mana (1W 1U + 4 gen) ✓, leaves 2U. Air: Aang 3/2 + Flyer 2/3 = 5. No Momo. 5 air vs Wasp blocker... 5 max if unblocked. Opp at 6. ✗ Not lethal. So Momo (discount + body) is essential. Line B it is.\n\
\n\
Also — wait, in Line B, Katara is tapped on their turn 9 and can't block; Momo must block the Wasp (flying) — Momo 1/1 flying CAN block Wasp 4/4 flying ✓ (flying blocks flying). Momo dies, I take 4 from Zookeeper → 3 life. Then Momo is DEAD on turn 10! No Momo → no discount, no 3/3 body!\n\
\n\
Oh no, I made an error. If Momo dies blocking on their turn 9, then turn 10: Aang {3}{W} (full price) + Flyer {1}{U} + Deserters {1}{W} = 8 mana, 3W needed ✗. Aang + Flyer = 6 mana ✓ (1W 1U + 4 gen), leaving 2U. Air: Aang 3/2 + Flyer 2/3 = 5 + Katara 3/4 ground. vs their blockers: if they attacked with both, everything tapped → 5 air + 3 ground = 8 ≥ 6 LETHAL ✓. If they held Wasp back: Wasp blocks Aang or Flyer → 2-3 through → opp at 3-4. ✗ not lethal. Then their turn 10: 22 power vs me at 3 (or 7 if they didn't attack). Dead.\n\
\n\
Hmm. So the question is whether they attack with both or hold Wasp back. If they attack with both (natural play — maximize damage, and from their view, tapping blockers doesn't matter because they have lethal next turn anyway... but wait, if they tap everything, I might have lethal — do they see it? My board turn 10: Katara 3/4 + whatever I cast. They don't know I have Aang/Flyer/Deserters. From their view: I have Katara 3/4, ~4-5 cards in hand, 8 lands. If they attack with both and tap out, and I have nothing, they win next turn anyway. If I have fliers... they might not respect it. Most players attack with both here.)\n\
\n\
But if they're clever: attack with Zookeeper only (keep Wasp as air blocker + Wasp is their best creature?). Then I take 4 (or Momo-blocks). Hmm, if Momo blocks Zookeeper: Momo dies, I stay at 7. Then turn 10: Aang {3}{W} + Flyer {1}{U} + Deserters... 3W ✗. Aang + Flyer = 5 air vs Wasp 4/4 blocker + Zookeeper tapped. Wasp blocks one → 2-3 through. Opp at 6-2=4 or 6-3=3. Not lethal. ✗.\n\
\n\
If I DON'T block Zookeeper with Momo: take 4 → 3 life, keep Momo 1/1. Turn 10: Aang {2}{W} + Flyer {1}{U} + Deserters {1}{W} = 7 mana ✓ (2W 1U + 4 gen... wait: Aang discounted {2}{W} = 1W + 2 gen; Flyer = 1U + 1 gen; Deserters = 1W + 1 gen. Total 7 mana, pips 2W 1U ✓ with 6U 2W). Momo → 3/3 (two ETB triggers), Deserters counter on Flyer → 3/4. Attack: Momo 3/3, Aang 3/2, Flyer 3/4 = 9 air. Wasp (untapped, held back) blocks one: any block → other two deal 6 → LETHAL ✓✓✓.\n\
\n\
So if they hold Wasp back and attack with Zookeeper only: I take 4 (don't block), go to 3, then win with the 3-flier attack (counter on Flyer). If they attack with both: Momo blocks Wasp (dies)... then turn 10 no Momo: Aang {3}{W} + Flyer {1}{U} = 6 mana, air = 5, everything tapped → 5 + Katara 3/4 ground = 8 ≥ 6 LETHAL ✓. Or Aang + Deserters (counter on Aang 4/3) + Flyer: Aang {3}{W} + Deserters {1}{W} = 6 mana (2W + 4 gen ✓), Flyer {1}{U} = 2 more = 8 total ✓✓ (2W 1U + 5 gen = 8 mana ✓). Air: Aang 4/3 + Flyer 2/3 = 6 → LETHAL exactly ✓. \n\
\n\
So:\n\
- They attack both turn 9: Momo blocks Wasp (dies), I take 4 → 3. Turn 10: Aang {3}{W} + Flyer {1}{U} + Deserters {1}{W} (8 mana ✓), counter on Aang → 4/3. Attack: Aang 4/3 + Flyer 2/3 = 6 air, everything tapped → 6 → LETHAL. ✓\n\
