\n\
Blockers: Katara (2/3, no flying), Momo (1/1, flying, summoning sick — sick creatures CAN block? No! Summoning sick creatures cannot attack or use tap abilities, but they CAN block. Wait, no — summoning sickness prevents attacking and activating abilities with tap/untap symbols. Blocking is allowed. Yes, Momo can block.\n\
\n\
So incoming: Bumi 5/4 trample, Buzzard-Wasp 4/4 flying, Zookeeper 4/4, Sozin 5/5 menace, Mountain 4/4. Total 22 power.\n\
\n\
My blocks: Momo can block Buzzard-Wasp (4/4 flying) — Momo dies, absorbs 4. Katara can block one ground creature: Bumi (trample — Katara 2/3 blocks, 5 trample damage: 2 to Katara... wait, trample assigns lethal to blocker (2 damage to Katara... actually 5/4 trample vs 2/3: assign 2 to Katara (lethal is 2... Katara has 3 toughness, so lethal is 3), must assign 3 to Katara before trampling over? Lethal damage = toughness = 3. So 3 to Katara, 2 trample to me. Hmm, actually 5 power, assign 3 to Katara (lethal), 2 to me. Then I take 2 + Zookeeper 4 + Sozin 5 + Mountain 4 = 15. Dead.\n\
\n\
Block Sozin with both? Sozin has menace, needs 2 blockers: Katara + Momo block Sozin (5/5). Sozin kills both (5 damage split: he assigns to both, both die). Then I take Bumi 5 (trample, all to me since unblocked) + Buzzard-Wasp 4 + Zookeeper 4 + Mountain 4 = 17. Dead.\n\
\n\
No matter what, if they attack with everything, I die. Unless... I can't do anything. All lands tapped, no instants in hand I can cast. Crashing Wave is likely a sorcery anyway (and I have no mana).\n\
\n\
Wait — do I have any tricks? Aang is a creature (sorcery speed). Jeong Jeong's Deserters creature. Island. Crashing Wave — need UU. No mana. So nothing.\n\
\n\
So I just pass and see what happens. Maybe they don't attack with everything? They'd be foolish not to — it's lethal. Actually let me double check: is it definitely lethal? I'm at 7. If they attack with all 5 creatures (22 power), I have 2 blockers that can absorb at most... Katara blocks a non-trampler: absorbs 4 (Zookeeper or Mountain). Momo blocks Buzzard-Wasp: absorbs 4. Then remaining: Bumi 5 (trample, unblocked = 5 to me), Sozin 5, other ground 4 = 14 to me. Dead.\n\
\n\
Best blocks: Katara blocks Bumi (trample: 3 to Katara... wait Katara is 2/3, lethal is 3, so 3 to Katara, 2 tramples), Momo blocks Buzzard-Wasp (4 absorbed, Momo dies). I take 2 + 5 (Sozin) + 4 (Zookeeper) + 4 (Mountain) = 15. Dead.\n\
\n\
Alternatively Katara blocks Sozin? Menace prevents single block. So no.\n\
\n\
So any attack with 3+ creatures probably kills me. Even just Bumi + Sozin + Buzzard-Wasp: block Buzzard with Momo, can't block Sozin alone with Katara... Katara blocks Bumi: take 2 + 5 = 7. Exactly dead. Or they just swing all.\n\
\n\
Hmm, so I'm dead unless opponent misplays. But wait — did I misplay by not keeping First-Time Flyer? It got exiled by Sold Out, couldn't help it.\n\
\n\
Actually, hold on. Let me reconsider. Should I have blocked differently earlier? Doesn't matter now. Let me just pass priority and see what they do. Maybe they don't have lethal because... no, they clearly have lethal. 22 power vs 7 life, I have 2 blockers.\n\
\n\
Actually wait, let me reconsider whether Momo is summoning sick — yes it shows summoning_sick: true, but that only prevents attacking/tap abilities, blocking is fine.\n\
\n\
OK so I pass. Nothing I can do. Let me also send a chat message since I should engage. Something like acknowledging the Sold Out play.\n\
\n\
Actually, before passing, let me double-check Crashing Wave's card type — if it's an instant, could I cast it? I have no untapped lands, so no regardless. Waterbend can pay the X generic with creature taps, but {U}{U} requires blue mana. No.\n\
\n\
And Aang? 3W — no mana. Deserters 1W — no mana. Island — not my turn, can't play land... actually it's opponent's turn, can't play lands.\n\
\n\
So pass priority. Let me send a chat message too.\n\
\n\
Let me think about what happens after: They attack, I block to minimize, but I die anyway. Actually, should I even block? If I'm dead no matter what, blocking doesn't matter. But maybe they only attack with some creatures. Let me pass and see the declare attackers step.\n\
\n\
Actually, one consideration: maybe they won't attack with Bumi because if Bumi deals combat damage to me, they get extra combat but I'm dead anyway. They'll just swing.\n\
\n\
Let me pass priority. I'llalso send a quick chat message.",
