        "wheeled": [],
        "pool_size": 0,
        "reasoning": "This is pick 1, pack 1 of a draft. Let me evaluate the cards.\n\
\n\
The set appears to be an Avatar: The Last Airbender themed set with mechanics like earthbend, airbend, waterbend, firebending.\n\
\n\
First pick considerations: I want a strong card, ideally a rare or strong uncommon, or something that keeps me open.\n\
\n\
Cards in the pack:\n\
1. Forest - basic land, never pick\n\
2. Badgermole {4}{G} - common, earthbend 2, trample to +1/+1 counter creatures\n\
3. First-Time Flyer {1}{U} - 2/1 flyer that gets +1/+1 with Lesson in graveyard, decent common\n\
4. Watery Grasp - tap down enchantment, weak-ish removal\n\
5. Aang's Journey {2} - ramp, gains 2 life\n\
6. Cat-Owl {3}{W/U} - 3/3-ish flyer? Untap artifact/creature\n\
7. Fire Nation Raider {3}{R} - raid clue token\n\
8. Foggy Bottom Swamp - B/G dual land, enters tapped, sac for card draw - this is a common fixing land\n\
9. Honest Work {U} - Uncommon, essentially removal: turns an opponent's creature into a 1/1 with no abilities. That's basically a 1-mana removal spell! Very strong.\n\
10. Glider Staff {2}{W} - equipment with airbend, decent\n\
11. Vengeful Villagers {3}{W} - tap down creature, stun counter potential\n\
12. Bitter Work {1}{R}{G} - two-color uncommon enchantment, draws cards\n\
13. South Pole Voyager {1}{W} - Rare, 2-mana (probably 2/2?) Ally with lifegain and card draw on second trigger. Depends on Allies synergy.\n\
14. Fire Lord Azula {1}{U}{B}{R} - three-color rare, copy spells when attacking. Strong but 3-color commitment first pick.\n\
\n\
Best candidates:\n\
- Honest Work: 1-mana removal that turns a creature into a 1/1 citizen that taps for colorless. It's cheap, flexible, mono-blue, and premium removal. Great first pick.\n\
- South Pole Voyager: rare, but only 2 mana and card draw requires two Ally ETBs per turn. Decent in an Ally deck but speculative.\n\
- Fire Lord Azula: powerful but Grixis 3-color, risky first pick.\n\
